      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Subtitles for any video\n\n1. Load a video with speech in **Video with speech**.\n2. Run. Qwen3-ASR writes down what is said, the forced aligner times every word, and Word Timestamps to Subtitles groups the words into subtitle lines.\n\nOutputs: an .srt file in `output/subtitles/`, a copy of the video with the subtitles burned in, in `output/video/`, and the plain transcript in the **Transcript** box. Burned-in subtitles draw Latin, Greek and Cyrillic letters; for other scripts use the .srt.\n\nThe language is detected; when detection picks the wrong one, set it in the speech to text node. Qwen3-ASR transcribes 30 languages, but its forced aligner times words in only 11: Chinese, English, Cantonese, French, German, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese, Russian and Spanish. For any other language, Finnish and Swedish among them, use *Subtitles from Speech (Whisper large-v3)*. `max_characters` and `max_seconds` decide how long one subtitle line gets."
      ],
      "title": "How to use"
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
